docs/USER_ID_CACHE_INVESTIGATION.md

app/frontend/tests/README-modal-test.md
docs/CI_TEST_FAILURES_ANALYSIS.md

# Codex CLI per-repo context, generated by ~/ai-company-brain/scripts/sync-configs.js
/AGENTS.md

# Date-prefixed working-log markdown files (per-task scratch notes under
# docs/task-management/, e.g. 2026-05-25-board-detail-edit-…md). Kept on
# disk for the author's reference, NOT committed. Pattern matches any
# YYYY-MM-DD-*.md file anywhere in the tree.
[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-*.md

# Session handoff notes (docs/task-management/HANDOFF-*.md). Same rationale as
# the dated working logs above: written for the next session to pick up a task,
# superseded once it does, and not a durable record. Durable lessons belong in
# docs/task-management/LEARNINGS.md, which IS committed.
HANDOFF-*.md
.cursor/rules/melissa-branch-workflow.mdc

# One-off generated artifacts (NotebookLM scripts, infographic/visual prompts,
# loose compliance journals/summaries). These are scratch for video/visual asset
# generation and belong in ~/ai-company-brain/outputs/, not the repo root. The
# durable, code-anchored compliance records live in docs/legal/ and audit-reports/
# (indexed by audit-reports/DOCUMENT-REGISTER.json).
/notebooklm-*
/*-prompt.txt
/*-prompt.md
/GET-STARTED-NOTEBOOKLM.md
/README-COMPLIANCE-VISUALS.md
/simple-text-visuals.md
/visual-creation-guide.md
/compliance-visuals-summary.md
/compliance-journal-*.md
/compliance-summary-*.md

# Playwright MCP session scratch
.playwright-mcp/

# Frontend scratchpad: local-only analysis/tooling scratch (one-off audit
# scripts, test-run logs, pre-merge file snapshots). Nothing here is part of
# the build; keep it out of the repo the same way per-task working logs are.
app/frontend/scratchpad/
